## 3. What should GitHub track vs ignore?

| Files | GitHub |
|---|---|
| React source code | <badge color="success">Track</badge> |
| Python source code | <badge color="success">Track</badge> |
| `package.json` | <badge color="success">Track</badge> |
| `package-lock.json` | <badge color="success">Track</badge> |
| `pyproject.toml` | <badge color="success">Track</badge> |
| `uv.lock` | <badge color="success">Track</badge> |
| NASA `.npy` files | <badge color="danger">Ignore</badge> |
| `node_modules` | <badge color="danger">Ignore</badge> |
| Python virtual environment | <badge color="danger">Ignore</badge> |
| `.env` secrets | <badge color="danger">Ignore</badge> |
| Trained model weights | <badge color="danger">Ignore</badge> |




